# Wave W17-Z (Route 216): drift post — a drift marker post where the drifts carve into waves: a snow-capped post with one carved drift mound banked at its foot, marking the causeway’s edge where the wind piles the pack (design: drifts carved into waves all along the snow bridge road). On pack turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s marker posts by the mound entire and from Route 217’s gear posts ahead by purpose: these mark where the snow moves, those mark where the climbers rest.
